 "context": "Current test axes c5, r4/r11. Previous attempt 4 grid was built by drawing full axes and filling rectangles interior-crossed: (r3-5,c4-6),(r3-7,c13-17),(r10-13,c1-5). It was marked wrong. Three demos all support this general rule. Need inspect subtleties: Could target be only cells that are 2 and connect to central cross intersection?",
 "tasks": [
  {
   "goal": "Check exact test cells and candidate #4 for missed component/coordinate. Report anything different.",
   "context": "Test rectangles and prior output described by parent. Third demo now shows rectangle r2-3,c7-9 at axes crosspoint corner fully becomes1.",
   "role": "leaf",
   "output_schema": {}
  },
  {
   "goal": "Find alternate plausible rule from three demos that would alter test output. Return output impact.",
   "context": "Demo1 two objects only horizontal/vertical rays internal filled; edge-touch remains line only. Demo2 internal vertical crossing fills. Demo3 object corner at intersection fills. Test uses two horizontal lines r4,11 and vertical c5.",
   "role": "leaf",
   "output_schema": {}
  }
 ],
 "role": "orchestrator",
 "output_schema": {},
